<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Colombo Plan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1950</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colombo">Colombo</a> Plan is a regional organisation for economic and social development in Asia and the Pacific, conceived at a meeting of Commonwealth foreign ministers in Colombo in 1950 and launched in 1951. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a> was a leading founder, and under the plan thousands of Asian students studied in Australian universities, helping to build ties with the region during the White Australia era.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/colombo-plan.jpg" alt="Colombo Plan" width="320" height="147" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bourenane Chahine · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Colombo_Plan_for_Cooperative_Economic_and_Social_Development_in_Asia_and_the_Pacific.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
